WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.969 line:8%
BEN ABBOTT: This is our
second chance tournament.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.004 line:14%
Up first, the runner-up duel.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.340
Both of you guys came
this close to winning

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:11.611
your rounds last time, but you
didn't quite seal the deal.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:15.515 line:14%
The duels start now.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.516 line:14%
 My name is Rick Rabjohn.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.251 line:14%
I'm 58 years old.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.854
The last time I was here, it
was the balance of my sword

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.089
that did me in.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.323
I wish I would have won.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.825
And that's why I'm
back here again today.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.760
Give it another go.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.196 line:14%
 I'm Michael Seronde.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.031 line:14%
I'm from Tucson, Arizona.

00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:34.367
Last time I was here,
It was so close.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.703
It would mean so much to me
if I make it through this duel

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.005
to the final round.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:42.241
I'd really love a second shot.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.076
 Since you guys both
came in second place

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:45.779
last time you were
here, we've decided

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.881
to make this competition
all about twos.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.650
Today, we do not want
you to make a blade,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:55.788
we want you to make two
different blades, a Damascus

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:58.023
dagger and a Damascus chopper.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.093
Your duel starts now.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.561
RICK RABJOHN: They're
two very different blade.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:05.064 line:8%
One built for, you know,
stabbing and slicing,

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.699 line:8%
and the other one,
built for chopping.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.235
Dagger is a little more
complicated than the chopper.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:13.339
I got the chopper to length
and pretty much to width.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.473
Ooh.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.942
As the clock is ticking,
I wish I was a little

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:19.311
bit further with these blades.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.614
But as I'm grinding,
I'm realizing

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.884
that, hey, you know what,
the forge walls went well,

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.086
I'm feeling pretty good.

00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:31.257
I'm going to move
on to the quench.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.894
 All right, well,
he's got one in there.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.196
Yay.

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:39.899
 I'm delighted I've
got to hardened blades.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.166
Now I got to temper it.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:44.003
 All right, Rick is
working on his handle.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.371
That's good.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.473
 I'm going to do full
tang, so, in this way,

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:51.176
I just put scales on
both sides of the tang

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:52.512
and leave it at that.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.713
I've got that done.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.748
Now, we work on this one.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.216
 He's got a handle
on his dagger,

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.986
and now, he's putting a
handle onto his chopper.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.387
RICK RABJOHN: As the
clock is ticking,

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:04.090
I still have a lot of work
to do to shape the handles

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.058
and put the final sharpening.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.426
It's going to come
right down to the wire,

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:10.195
but I'm confident
I'm going to make it.

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:11.497 line:14%
 We got Rick etching.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.065 line:14%
 Oh, good.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.766 line:14%
 Right on.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.200 line:14%
You can color me impressed.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.669
Told him to make two blades.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.371
That is one hell of a feat.

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.240
 Biggest concern
is making two knives

00:02:21.306 --> 00:02:23.809
out of Damascus in five hours.

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:24.810
That's out of control.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.279
I've never done that before.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.381
Instead of just sitting
looking at the steel heat up,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.650
I have time to get my
handle materials ready.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.719
 Look how much Mike has
already accomplished.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:37.624
 [inaudible] drawn out to
almost being blade size.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.697
 At this point, my knives
are really taking shape.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:45.632
They look solid.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.366
Now, it's time to quench.

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:48.734
The time constraints
are a little bit

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.904
challenging, heat treating
two blades back to back.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:55.308
I need to nail my heat treat.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.676
Boom.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.444
After quenching my chopper, I
don't think it's hard enough.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:02.882
This file doesn't skate quite
as easily as I wanted to.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.083
HOST: Second quench.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.585
Put some bunch of
stress on his blade.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.154
 I have to do it again.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.388
This time, it works.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.924
I don't have any
more time to waste.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.793
It's time to move
on to the dagger.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.094
It's a little bit thinner.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.595
It has two cutting edges.

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:19.165
So I have to make sure
that heat is even more

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:23.068
even than it was in my chopper.

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:25.505
 All right, dagger is quenched.

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.672
 It's straight.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.575
I've got a chunk of
mesquite wood from earlier.

00:03:29.641 --> 00:03:32.879
And I have to attach
handles to two knives.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.914
There is a lot of work to
do in not very much time.

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:37.249
I've got to get going.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.120
I have a dagger on a 2
inch square block handle.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.722
That is not going to fly.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:48.127
I blast through the block trying
to get that handle to something

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:49.896
that is comfortable enough.

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.031
Key is enough.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.866
I'm trying to dribble
a little bit of glue

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:57.670
because I'm afraid I don't have
enough epoxy to make everything

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.938
stick together right.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.941
I'm at the grinder with both
my dagger and my chopper.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:05.410
At this stage, I feel like
I'm sprinting between tasks,

00:04:05.477 --> 00:04:07.780
and I keep bouncing
between these two knives.

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:15.321
 Five, four, three, two, one.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.056
Gentlemen, turn
off the machines.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.725
Put down your tools.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.425
This duel is over.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.025
[claps]

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:22.562
 Good job.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.198
 [exhales]

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.299
 All right, runners up,
it's time for our doubled up

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:30.903
strength test, stab and chop.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:33.639
I'm going to take your daggers,
stab them into a stump here.

00:04:33.705 --> 00:04:35.541
And then I'll take your
choppers and attack

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:38.210
both the post and the skulls.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.579
Michael, you're
up first on this.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.213
Are you ready?

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.414
 Ah, yes.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.290
OK.

00:04:59.431 --> 00:05:00.433
 [whispers] It didn't break.

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.468
 It did not break.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.603
 All right, Mike,
start with your dagger.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:08.040
Right off, the weight and
feel of this blade, I mean,

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.041
this is super comfortable.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.342
I could play with this all day.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.077
It's got a wicked edge
and a wicked point

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:13.379
on it, which I really like.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.446
I poked it in there.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:17.083
It dug in deep and held up fine.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:20.419
What I don't like is that
leather spacer you put in here,

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.721
you then covered
it with Krazy Glue.

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:25.491
That turned it into
some sharp edges.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.426
When you're thrusting
into something,

00:05:27.492 --> 00:05:29.661
it's not really a good thing.

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:33.399
As far as your chopper goes,
again, nice weight on this.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.667
You didn't take
really any damage.

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.871
This is still a
wicked sharp blade.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.706
So all in all, nice set.

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.273
Well done.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.541
 Thank you.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:43.976
 All right, Rick,
you're up next.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:44.776
You good?

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:45.411
 Yeah.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.646
 All right, let's do it.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:49.115
[music playing]

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.864
 [claps] That's great.

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:09.602
 So right off the bat,
this is a heavy dagger.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.637
There's a lot of metal there.

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:15.908
Um, what really got me was
all this right around here,

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.844
there are kind of
sharp jagged edges.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.380
And since the handle doesn't
really have any contouring,

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.149
there's no way to
keep off that guard.

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:28.488
Now, on your chopper, again,
that's a lot of material there.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:32.057
But it does have an edge, and
that edge didn't take damage.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.359
So that's great.

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:35.628
They held up very, very well.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:36.295
So good job.

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:37.397
 Thank you.

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:43.503
 All right, bladesmiths, we
know your weapons are strong,

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.037
but are they sharp?

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:49.842
This is the water tube slice and
the canvas bag stab and slice.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.610
To find out how sharp
your weapons are,

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.346
we'll take your weapons and
slash across these water

00:06:54.446 --> 00:06:55.915
tubes and canvas bag.

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.951
Double your weapons, double
the slice, double the nice.

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.552
[laughter]

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:02.088
Mike, you're up first.
Are you ready for this?

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.022
 Oh, yeah.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:03.989
 All right, let's do this.

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:06.626
[music playing]

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.103
 Ooh.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:18.904
 Beautiful.

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.239
 [laughs] [claps]

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:25.377
 All right, Michael, off the
bat, these feel really good.

00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:28.480
Even though they are
two different designs,

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.950
they feel equally
balanced on both hands,

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:32.884
and they are wicked sharp.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:36.755
On the slash on the water
tubes, very clean slice.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:38.424
You have a sharp edge here, sir.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:42.061
Also, on the stabbing and
slashing with your dagger,

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:43.829
those are very clean cuts.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:46.998
Overall, sir, both your
weapons, they will cut.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.434
 [laughs] Sweet.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.102
HOST: All right, Rick,
are you ready, sir?

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:50.836
 No.

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:51.370
No.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:52.605
[laughter]

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:53.672
 Well, we're going
to do it anyways.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:54.406
 We're going to do it.
[laughter]

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:57.109
[music playing]

00:08:12.424 --> 00:08:13.325
 [laughs]

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:14.760
 [exhales]

00:08:14.826 --> 00:08:16.795
 All right, Rick, let's
talk about your weapons here.

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:19.932
First up, these
are heavy beasts.

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:23.402
And even for a dagger, it's
very forward heavy weight.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:25.905
Same with your chopper,
as a chopper is expected.

00:08:25.971 --> 00:08:29.608
For a dagger, it's
very heavy, but I

00:08:29.674 --> 00:08:31.510
was still able to cut cleanly.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:34.279
You have a sharp edge
on your chopper here.

00:08:34.379 --> 00:08:36.414
Overall, sir, they will cut.

00:08:36.481 --> 00:08:37.048
 Thank you.

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:38.049
HOST: Good job.

00:08:38.116 --> 00:08:40.585
 Thank you.

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:41.754
 Very well done, gentlemen.

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.722
[laughter]

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:45.191
But only one of you
guys can leave here

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:47.126
with a check for
$2,000 and a spot

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:50.496
in the final leg of this
second chance tournament.

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:56.067
The bladesmith who won
this duel is Michael.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:57.469
Congratulations.

00:08:57.569 --> 00:08:59.171
You're moving forward
into the final round

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:00.539
of the second shot tournament.

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.574
Unfortunately, Rick,
that means you're

00:09:02.674 --> 00:09:03.909
not going to be moving forward.

00:09:03.975 --> 00:09:05.477
I'm going to have to
ask you to please leave.

00:09:05.544 --> 00:09:07.112
 OK, take care, man.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:07.913
I'll see you.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:08.880
Good job.

00:09:08.947 --> 00:09:10.715
Last time my
competitors blade was

00:09:10.815 --> 00:09:12.451
just better balanced than mine.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.186
I still can't get it right.

00:09:14.287 --> 00:09:15.787
I agree with the
judge's decision,

00:09:15.887 --> 00:09:18.156
but I'm also proud of what
I accomplished in getting

00:09:18.256 --> 00:09:19.658
through this tough challenge.

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:21.893
It was fun and always good
to meet other bladesmiths.

00:09:21.993 --> 00:09:23.629
And once again, it's
been a great experience.

00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:26.832
And if there's a third
chance tournament, I'm in.

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:28.633
 Michael, congratulations, man.

00:09:28.733 --> 00:09:30.536
That means you broke
the second place curse,

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:32.905
and you came out on top
of your duel, which also

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:34.941
means you're moving forward
into the final round

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:36.108
of our tournament.

00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:38.377
And you are leaving here
with a check for $2,000,

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:40.111
so congratulations,
man, very well done.

00:09:40.178 --> 00:09:40.946
 Thank you.

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:42.814
Thank you.

00:09:42.914 --> 00:09:45.217
 We will see you for the
second round of this tournament.

00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:47.753
 Winning feels incredible.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.222
This challenge was
the hardest smithing

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:51.724
challenge I've ever done.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:54.759
Knowing that, I can't even
begin to imagine what's next.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.163
The next stage of
this competition

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:58.831
is going to be that much harder.

00:09:58.897 --> 00:10:02.435
Every one of the smiths in the
next round have already won.

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:04.569
So I know they're going
to bring their best.

00:10:04.636 --> 00:10:06.138
I have to bring my best.

00:10:06.205 --> 00:10:07.805
It's going to be brutal.

